.TH SIREN 1 "2026-06-27" "S.I.R.E.N" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
siren \- Linux memory acquisition tool with audit-aware triage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo ./src/siren.sh
[\fI--quick\fR | \fI--full\fR | \fI--test\fR | \fI--map\fR]
[\fI--output\fR \fIdir\fR]
[\fI--help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
S.I.R.E.N (Shell Interactive Runtime Entity Notifier) performs
forensic memory acquisition on Linux systems. It reads
/proc/kcore using ELF-aware extraction (via Python) or dd
fallback, generates SHA256 checksums, extracts strings, and
produces JSON/CSV reports with chain-of-custody metadata.
It can optionally consume LinSpec audit reports to adapt
acquisition parameters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--quick
Quick triage dump: capture first 100 MB of /proc/kcore via dd.
.TP
.B \--full
Full acquisition: ELF-aware extraction of PT_LOAD segments
from /proc/kcore (requires python3).
.TP
.B \--test
Test acquisition pipeline by reading /proc/version.
.TP
.B \--map
Display system RAM regions from /proc/iomem.
.TP
.B \--output \fIdir\fR
Custom output directory for dumps and reports.
.TP
.B \--help
Display this help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I LINSPEC_REPORT
Path to a LinSpec report.json for audit-aware acquisition.
.TP
.I SIREN_LINSPEC_REPORT
Alternative to LINSPEC_REPORT.
.TP
.I SIREN_DUMPS_DIR
Override the default dumps directory (default: <project>/dumps).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/kcore
Source for memory acquisition.
.TP
.I dumps/
Output directory for binary dumps, reports, and checksums.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, 1 on error.
.SH AUTHOR
Jefferson Cesar Antunes
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linspec (1),
.BR kscanner (1),
.BR kcore (5)
